    { "id": "thesis", "page": "page-1", "x": 0, "y": -150, "w": 700,
      "text": "Same tokens as tokens.css — nothing invented.\nThe change is where the chrome goes: a left rail on desktop and a tab bar on phone, so the top of every screen is content instead of controls." },
    { "id": "phone-note", "page": "page-1", "x": 3120, "y": -150, "w": 390,
      "text": "Five rows of controls became one.\nToday ~55% of a 390px screen is chrome before the first cover." },
    { "id": "dark-note", "page": "page-2", "x": 0, "y": -170, "w": 700,
      "text": "A token swap, exactly as the app does it — every value is the dark counterpart already defined in tokens.css.\nTwo things deliberately do not invert: cover artwork, and the rendered PDF page (PDF.js paints the real document, which is white paper).\nDepth comes from borders here rather than shadow, per the note in tokens.css." },
    { "id": "dark-phone-note", "page": "page-2", "x": 3120, "y": -150, "w": 390,
